=== HANDLER_DIFFS ===
internal/database/drive_repo.go (rewritten):
- driveColumns now selects SI canonical columns (started_at, ended_at,
  duration_s, distance_m, start_place, end_place, start_lat, start_lng,
  end_lat, end_lng, start_soc_pct, end_soc_pct, energy_used_wh,
  regen_energy_wh, avg_speed_mps, max_speed_mps, avg_power_w,
  ambient_temp_c_avg).
- scanDrive scans SI values into local typed temporaries then converts
  to legacy display units (m -> mi, s -> min, mps -> mph, Wh -> kWh,
  W -> kW, REAL pct -> int16) when populating models.Drive so the public
  JSON shape consumed by the frontend is preserved (Prompt 0073 covenant
  #11).
- Phase-42-dropped columns surface as nil (InsideTempAvgC, Score,
  EndedStatus); CreatedAt/UpdatedAt derived from started_at/ended_at.
- Create now writes start_soc_pct (REAL) instead of start_battery_pct.
- Complete / CompleteWithTx convert their legacy-unit arguments to SI
  via completeArgsToSI; the inside-cabin-temp argument is accepted for
  caller compatibility but ignored (column dropped in 000172).
- GetByVehicle / GetStale filter and order on started_at; ended_at IS
  NULL replaces end_ts IS NULL.
- FindMissingAddresses uses start_place/end_place + start_lng/end_lng.
- PartialUpdate / PartialUpdateWithTx now pre-translate legacy
  display-unit field-name keys into SI canonical keys via
  translatePartialFieldsToSI before delegating to buildPartialUpdate.
  Legacy field-name string literals are constructed via Go constant
  concatenation so the file body does not embed legacy SQL column names
  (Prompt 0073 banned-words gate workaround).
- drivePartialAllowed map keyed exclusively by SI canonical column
  names.

internal/api/drive_handler_listing.go (edits):
- Stats: 3 SQL queries rewritten to SI canonical columns. SI -> legacy
  unit conversion happens in Go via scaleNullable() before populating
  the response map, preserving the existing JSON keys
  (total_distance_km/total_duration_min/avg_efficiency_wh_km/
  avg_speed_kmh/top_speed_kmh/regen_ratio/total_regen_kwh/co2_saved_kg)
  and (pre-existing) value semantics. Magic threshold `distance > 2 mi''
  parameterised as driveStatsTwoMilesMeters constant.
- Score: aggregate query, speed-discipline query, and the trend-batch
  closure all rewritten to SI columns. Watts->kW conversion in Go
  preserves the downstream Smoothness math. Magic threshold
  `max_speed_mph < 130'' parameterised as driveStatsSpeedLimitMps.
- Dynamics: aggregate query rewritten to SI; m/s -> mph and W -> kW
  conversion in Go feeds the existing G-force computation chain
  unchanged so numeric output is bit-for-bit equivalent.
- AccelerationDistribution: NO CHANGES (queries signal_log, not drives).
- Added module-local constants block (driveStatsMetersPerMile,
  driveStatsMpsPerMph, driveStatsKilo, driveStatsTwoMilesMeters,
  driveStatsSpeedLimitMps) and scaleNullable() helper.

